{
  "reviews": {
    "node-1vihicz": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims a pressure drop from ~6.8 bar to below alarm thresholds (<4.5 bar) at the receiving header (P-R). The evidence packet contains no direct measurement record for P-R showing this specific transition or confirming that 10:00 AM was when it occurred; IA-P01 is explicitly described as sampled values, not a continuous waveform covering all locations.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A pressure extract or sensor log specifically capturing the time-series value at location P-R around 10:00 AM on May 20, 2024 that shows the drop from ~6.8 bar to below 4.5 bar.","question":"Does a continuous waveform or high-frequency sample exist for header P-R between 09:55 and 10:05 showing the pressure transition?"
    },
    "node-1d8qtyz": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    },
    "node-ng9a3s": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node asserts that the maintenance acceptance signature was not yet signed at notification time. The evidence excerpt (IA-S02) states 'Maintenance acceptance signature: not yet signed at notification time' but explicitly qualifies this as a work-stage record and clarifies it is 'not evidence that any particular field valve was open or closed.' Treating an unsigned administrative field as proof of procedural status without establishing the requirement for such a signature before proceeding constitutes upgrading a missing record into proof of absence.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A documented procedure specifying when (or if) maintenance acceptance signatures are required prior to work boundary preparation, and evidence that this specific step was mandated at 09:31 or earlier.","question":"Is there an applicable requirement stating the maintenance acceptance signature must be completed before initiating field execution for WO-527-E?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Two of three proposed nodes lack sufficient evidence support. Node node-1vihicz lacks a direct measurement record confirming the pressure drop at P-R; IA-P01 is insufficient due to sampling limitations and missing location coverage. Node node-ng9a3s relies on an administrative field status without establishing whether that signature was a prerequisite for work, risking misinterpretation of 'missing' as 'violation.' Only node-1d8qtyz regarding the blank execution record is supported by direct text.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1", "IA-I01"],
    "unknowns": [
      "Actual pressure value and time of drop at P-R.",
      "Whether a signature was required before work initiation."
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "The alarm may have been triggered by upstream conditions not captured in the provided samples.",
      "Work could have proceeded without requiring an acceptance signature, making node-ng9a3s irrelevant to causality."
    ],"confidence": 0.75}
  }
